---
import Layout from "@layouts/default.astro";
import "@styles/long-text-content.css";
import Headline from "@components/headline.astro";
import { useTranslations } from "@utils/i18n";
import { themeConfig } from '~/theme.config';

const locale = themeConfig.i18n.defaultLocale;
const t = useTranslations(locale);

const updated = "13 August 2026";
---

<Layout title={t('pages.privacy-policy.title')} robots="noindex, follow" header={{ showTopBanner: false }}>
  <Headline text={t('pages.privacy-policy.title')} class="pb-10" />

  <div class="long-text-content text-left wrap-break-word">
    <p class="text-stone-500 italic dark:text-stone-300">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      amoris.in is a static website. There is no account to create, no login, and no form on this site that stores what you type. This page describes the only data that is actually collected, and why.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>We use two analytics tools to understand which pages are read and where people give up:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> - aggregate traffic data: pages viewed, approximate location at country or city level, device and browser type, and how you arrived. IP addresses are anonymised by Google before storage.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> - anonymised session data such as scroll depth and clicks, used to find pages where the layout is failing people.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Both tools set cookies in your browser. Neither is used to build an advertising profile of you, and we do not sell or share this data with anyone.
    </p>

    <h3>When you get in touch</h3>
    <p>
      If you email, message on WhatsApp, or book a call, we hold whatever you send us for as long as needed to have that conversation and any work that follows. Calls are booked through Calendly and video calls run on third-party platforms; those services handle your data under their own privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h3>Hosting</h3>
    <p>
      The site is served from our own server. Standard web server logs record IP address, timestamp and requested URL, which is necessary to serve the page and to spot abuse. These logs are not used for analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not sell personal data.</li>
      <li>We do not run advertising or retargeting pixels.</li>
      <li>We do not add you to a mailing list because you visited the site.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can block analytics cookies in your browser settings, or use a content blocker, and the site will work exactly the same. Most browsers also offer a "Do Not Track" setting.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can ask what data we hold about you, ask for a copy, or ask us to delete it. Email <a href="mailto:shahi@amoris.in">shahi@amoris.in</a> and we will respond within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties referenced on this site</h2>
    <p>
      Links out to GitHub, npm, LinkedIn, Calendly and WhatsApp are ordinary links. Once you follow one, that service's own privacy policy applies and this one no longer does.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Amoris, Bengaluru, India<br />
      <a href="mailto:shahi@amoris.in">shahi@amoris.in</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
